// Solstice, Hex's own look. A plum slate where most dark editors are a blue grey, the neutrals leaning the way of the
// accent, and one accent a mode: this is Dawn's, the orange of Hex's icon, and solstice_dusk has Dusk's violet over the
// same ground. The accent says where you are and what is running and nothing else, a warning is its own yellow so it
// is never taken for it. Hex draws a Solstice window flush, its panes against each other with no gaps and no round
// (HexLooks.Flush), the controls in them still round.
let theme = {
    title: "Solstice",
    background: vec(0.094, 0.090, 0.122, 1),
    surface: vec(0.125, 0.122, 0.165, 1),
